pat:DirectPromptingMotif a pair:GraphMotif ;
    rdfs:label "Direct Prompting Motif"@en ;
    dct:description """
    Architectural motif in which a user query is handled directly by a
    generative model step and produces a user-facing answer. 
    """@en ;
    dct:source <https://martinfowler.com/articles/gen-ai-patterns/> ;
    pair:derivedFrom <https://martinfowler.com/articles/gen-ai-patterns/> ;
    pair:hasPatternEdge pat:DP_GenerationProducesAnswerEdge,
        pat:DP_GenerationUsesModelEdge,
        pat:DP_GenerationUsesQueryEdge ;
    pair:hasPatternNode pat:DP_AnswerNode,
        pat:DP_GenerationStepNode,
        pat:DP_ModelNode,
        pat:DP_QueryNode ;
    pair:hasRiskPattern pat:DirectPromptingWithoutGroundingRiskPattern,
        pat:ImproperOutputHandlingRiskPattern,
        pat:PromptInjectionRiskPattern,
        pat:UnboundedConsumptionRiskPattern ;
    pair:implementedBy pat:DP_MatchingOQP ;
    skos:scopeNote """
    Direct Prompting is linked to these risk patterns because the
    motif represents user input flowing directly into a generative model and
    producing user-facing output without an explicit retrieval or grounding
    step. This makes prompt-context manipulation, unsupported generation,
    unvalidated generated output, and unbounded model use relevant conditions
    to test. The mapping does not assert that every Direct Prompting instance
    is risky; each risk pattern still requires its applicability condition and
    executable OQP to be satisfied during assessment.
    """@en .

pat:DirectPromptingWithoutGroundingOQP a pair:PatternImplementation ;
    rdfs:label "Direct Prompting without grounding risk pattern OQP"@en ;
    pair:implementationPath "ontology/patterns/implementation/risk_direct_prompting_without_grounding.rq" ;
    pair:implementsRiskPattern pat:DirectPromptingWithoutGroundingRiskPattern ;
    pair:producesOutputType pair:RiskFinding ;
    skos:altLabel "Direct LLM answering without grounding risk pattern OQP"@en .

